On the twenty-sixth day of my internship, I started studying 
the basics of computer networking in a Linux environment. 
I read the networking-related sections from the Linux book 
and learned about IP addresses, ports, localhost, TCP, UDP, 
and DNS.

I also learned about the purpose of the ping command and
reviewed how the localhost address is used to refer to the 
local computer. In addition, I looked at the ip command and 
studied how it can provide information about network interfaces 
and IP addresses.

These topics helped me understand the networking concepts that
I had previously encountered while working with SSH 
and OverTheWire. I also reviewed some additional Linux 
networking resources to reinforce the information from the book.
